exports[`formatSgeQuickscan pins > renders every branch exactly [compact] 1`] = `
{
  "abstaining": "NZ SGE: abstain.example — INDETERMINATE — this is NOT a pass and NOT a failure. One or more controls could not be measured, so SGE compliance can be neither confirmed nor denied for this domain.
0 satisfied | 0 not satisfied | 7 not measured (of 7)
No check completed for this domain, so NONE of the six SGE controls were measured. Every control below is reported as NOT MEASURED — the absence of a verdict, never a pass and never a requirement found unmet.
SMTP transport TLS (control 4 of 7) is NOT MEASURED here: this scanner reads DNS and HTTPS and never opens an SMTP session, so it never observes whether a mail exchanger negotiates TLS. A DNS-only result can therefore never be COMPLIANT — INDETERMINATE is the ceiling, and INDETERMINATE is not a pass. Supply a transport observation from an SMTP probe to decide this control.
Full sub-domain coverage (control 7 of 7) is NOT MEASURED here: SGE requires EVERY sub-domain to publish its own _dmarc record, v=spf1 -all and a null v=DKIM1; p= record — and it does not accept sp= at the apex as the remedy — but this tool enumerates no sub-domains, so it measured none of them. That is the absence of a verdict, NOT a finding that the sub-domains are protected and NOT a finding that they are exposed. Supply a sub-domain enumeration to decide this control.

 ? DMARC: NOT MEASURED — no verdict was reached (neither a pass nor a failure) — the check did not complete (timeout or error), so nothing was observed.
 ? SPF: NOT MEASURED — no verdict was reached (neither a pass nor a failure) — the check did not complete (timeout or error), so nothing was observed.
 ? DKIM: NOT MEASURED — no verdict was reached (neither a pass nor a failure) — the check did not complete (timeout or error), so nothing was observed.
 ? SMTP TLS: NOT MEASURED — no verdict was reached (neither a pass nor a failure) — this scanner never opens an SMTP session, so transport TLS is never observed here.
 ? MTA-STS: NOT MEASURED — no verdict was reached (neither a pass nor a failure) — the check did not complete (timeout or error), so nothing was observed.
 ? TLS-RPT: NOT MEASURED — no verdict was reached (neither a pass nor a failure) — the check did not complete (timeout or error), so nothing was observed.
 ? Sub-domain coverage: NOT MEASURED — no verdict was reached (neither a pass nor a failure) — no sub-domain enumeration was supplied, so no sub-domain was measured. This is the ABSENCE OF A MEASUREMENT, not a finding that the sub-domains are unprotected.",
  "bad": "NZ SGE: bad.example — NOT COMPLIANT — at least one SGE control was measured and found unmet.
1 satisfied | 4 not satisfied | 2 not measured (of 7)
SMTP transport TLS (control 4 of 7) is NOT MEASURED here: this scanner reads DNS and HTTPS and never opens an SMTP session, so it never observes whether a mail exchanger negotiates TLS. A DNS-only result can therefore never be COMPLIANT — INDETERMINATE is the ceiling, and INDETERMINATE is not a pass. Supply a transport observation from an SMTP probe to decide this control.
Full sub-domain coverage (control 7 of 7) is NOT MEASURED here: SGE requires EVERY sub-domain to publish its own _dmarc record, v=spf1 -all and a null v=DKIM1; p= record — and it does not accept sp= at the apex as the remedy — but this tool enumerates no sub-domains, so it measured none of them. That is the absence of a verdict, NOT a finding that the sub-domains are protected and NOT a finding that they are exposed. Supply a sub-domain enumeration to decide this control.

 ✗ DMARC: NOT SATISFIED
 ✗ SPF: NOT SATISFIED
 ✓ DKIM: SATISFIED
 ? SMTP TLS: NOT MEASURED — no verdict was reached (neither a pass nor a failure) — this scanner never opens an SMTP session, so transport TLS is never observed here.
 ✗ MTA-STS: NOT SATISFIED
